  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The dehydration of alcohol takes place via the formation of a&nbsp;carbocation. Hence, the rate of reaction depends on the stability of carbocation.</p><p>No dehydration is possible in phenol because carbocation formation is difficult in case of phenol.</p><p>Option (d) fast due to loss of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;conjugation increasing stable of compound as compared to (c). Option(b) is very fast because stable compound formed.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
    "image": null
  },
